-- ============================================================
-- GEOGRAPHY SEED — Maharashtra, FULL hierarchy from LGD source
-- State -> District -> Taluka (subdistrict) -> Village
-- Source: Local Government Directory (lgdirectory.gov.in) mirror
--   https://github.com/planemad/india-local-government-directory
--   administrative/{2-district,3-subdistrict,4-village}.csv
--   downloaded 2026-08-04. 36 districts / 355 talukas / 43,732
--   unique inhabited villages (Un-Inhabitant hamlets excluded).
-- pin_code is NULL for every village — LGD does not carry postal
--   codes; do not fabricate them, backfill from India Post data
--   separately if needed.
-- District names for Ahmednagar/Aurangabad/Osmanabad are mapped
--   to their current official names (Ahilyanagar/Chhatrapati
--   Sambhajinagar/Dharashiv) to match seed_maharashtra_geography.sql
--   and seed_maharashtra_districts_talukas_all.sql. Taluka names
--   here are the LGD spellings and may not exactly match the
--   hand-typed ones in seed_maharashtra_districts_talukas_all.sql
--   (e.g. North Solapur vs LGD spelling) — prefer THIS file as the
--   authoritative one; the older districts+talukas-only file can
--   be dropped once this is applied.
-- Idempotent via INSERT IGNORE plus the schema UNIQUE KEY
--   (state_id,name)/(district_id,name) constraints. Villages have
--   no unique constraint, so this file de-dupes exact
--   (taluka,name) pairs itself before emitting INSERTs.
-- ============================================================

SET NAMES utf8mb4;

SET @mh = (SELECT id FROM states WHERE code = 'MH');

